ref	plugins/soleur/test/preflight-check10-suite-integrity.test.sh	README.md	plugins/soleur/skills/deepen-plan/workflows/deepen-plan.workflow.js:254	f2cbe25fbf5e/1	- observability (applicable ONLY when the plan's Files-to-Edit touch production code/infra — i.e. NOT pure-docs: not all paths under knowledge-base/, docs/, README.md, CHANGELOG.md, or *.md outside plugins/*/skills and apps/*): a \x5c`## Observability\x5c` section with all 5 fields (liveness_signal, error_reporting, failure_modes, logs, discoverability_test), no placeholder values (TODO/TBD/N/A/placeholder/"manual operator check"), no empty field, and discoverability_test.command must NOT require ssh. It must also be executable by preflight Check 10, which runs it in a sandbox behind a deny-by-default allowlist: the first whitespace-delimited token of its dequoted, normalized value is one of curl bash grep rg jq python3 node bun printf git, with no path-shaped exemption. The OPTIONAL discoverability_test.credentials_required sub-field declares a probe whose property has no unauthenticated substitute ("<scope> — <justification>"), making Check 10 skip without executing; it is checked only when present, must not be placeholder text, and does NOT override the ssh reject. Two further rejects (#8412) bind ONLY a discoverability_test this run authors or amends — against a pre-existing block, report them as findings and leave satisfied unchanged: (a) command must be able to finish inside Check 10's 15-second `timeout 15s` cap, so a whole test suite or full build is rejected (wrapping a suite in a script satisfies the verb allowlist, not the cap); (b) expected_output must be the LITERAL string(s) the command prints, not prose describing them, because Check 10 asks whether any token of expected_output is a substring of stdout and a sentence can never match. If pure-docs, applicable=false, satisfied=true.
