ref	plugins/soleur/scripts/sync-pr-behind.test.sh	plugins/soleur/skills/ship/references/merge-queue-dequeue.md	plugins/soleur/scripts/sync-pr-behind.sh:402	09baea21c034/1	printf '%s' "PR #$PR is BEHIND, auto-merge is armed (not in the queue yet) and $b has a merge queue: not syncing — a resync alone restarts every required check and the queue makes the PR current. Wait for MERGED or a dequeue$poll. Red required check? Push the fix itself, not a resync. $hand Green and never enqueued? Follow plugins/soleur/skills/ship/references/merge-queue-dequeue.md ('Armed and green but never enqueued')."
ref	plugins/soleur/scripts/sync-pr-behind.test.sh	plugins/soleur/skills/ship/references/merge-queue-dequeue.md	plugins/soleur/scripts/sync-pr-behind.sh:570	7b7d1b90e86f/1	tag dequeued 13 "PR #$PR was in the merge queue and is no longer (OPEN, $am, $reason): a failed merge_group run or a removal — NOT syncing. Recover (ONE re-enqueue, procedure: plugins/soleur/skills/ship/references/merge-queue-dequeue.md): (1) read why: gh run list --event merge_group --limit 100 --json databaseId,headBranch,headSha,conclusion,url --jq '.[] | select(.headBranch | startswith(\x5c"gh-readonly-queue/main/pr-$PR-\x5c"))' then gh run view <databaseId> --log-failed — under grouped merging (max_entries_to_merge=3) a member PR's group ref names the DEEPEST member, so if no run matches pr-$PR- list recent merge_group runs and correlate by headSha/createdAt; (2) fix on the branch, git merge origin/main, push; (3) re-arm once: gh pr merge $PR --squash --auto. A second dequeue: stop and report it."
