ref	.claude/hooks/git-commit-secret-scan.test.sh	knowledge-base/project/learnings/security-issues/2026-05-25-terraform-show-json-leaks-sensitive-variables-into-fixtures.md	.claude/hooks/git-commit-secret-scan.sh:971	9513c25b12b4/1	reason="BLOCKED: gitleaks found ${findings_count} secret-shaped string(s) in the staged index of ${repo_s}. Locations: ${findings_summary}. The default action is to scrub the secrets — never commit-then-rotate. Recovery: (1) unstage the offending file(s) in ${repo_s} with 'git restore --staged <path>'; (2) redact the secret bytes in place; (3) re-stage and retry. If the staged content is a captured-real fixture from 'terraform show -json' or similar, strip the '.variables' block — terraform-show-json embeds sensitive HCL variables verbatim regardless of sensitive=true. See knowledge-base/project/learnings/security-issues/2026-05-25-terraform-show-json-leaks-sensitive-variables-into-fixtures.md."
